---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Failure Modes - Sthenos">
  <nav>
    <a href="/">Sthenos</a>
    <a href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
    <a href="/drill">Drill</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="section" style="background-image: url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534796636912-3b95b3ab5986?w=1920&q=80');">
    <div class="content">
      <p class="label">03_failure_modes.html</p>
      <h1>Failure Modes & Risk</h1>
      <p>Critical vulnerabilities that could compromise system reliability. Understanding where the system fails is as important as understanding what it does.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="fail-grid">
      <div class="fail-item critical">
        <span class="fail-num">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Data Sparsity</h3>
          <p>Insufficient breadcrumbs → incomplete trajectory reconstruction. Errors propagate through all downstream stages.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fail-item">
        <span class="fail-num">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Terrain Mis-modeling</h3>
          <p>Terrain cost field inaccuracies → suboptimal path inference.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fail-item">
        <span class="fail-num">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Behavioral Misclassification</h3>
          <p>Static/streaming divergence → entity role errors.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fail-item">
        <span class="fail-num">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Rule Brittleness</h3>
          <p>Rule thresholds fail on novel tactical scenarios.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fail-item warning">
        <span class="fail-num">05</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Metric Illusion</h3>
          <p>F1 > 70% but eval on synthetic data only — real gap unknown.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box" style="margin-top: 64px;">
      <h3>Error Amplification</h3>
      <p>Small errors in ingestion compound through inference. A 5% location error can become 20% behavioral misclassification.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 24px 5%;
    z-index: 100;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(0,0,0,0.8) 0%, transparent 100%);
  }

  nav a {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1.17px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .content-section {
    background: var(--space-black);
    padding: 80px 5%;
  }

  .fail-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .fail-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--ghost-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--ghost-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .fail-item.critical {
    border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.5);
    background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.1);
  }

  .fail-item.warning {
    border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.5);
    background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.1);
  }

  .fail-num {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 700;
    opacity: 0.2;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 13px;
    opacity: 0.7;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .insight-box {
    background: var(--ghost-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--ghost-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 32px;
  }

  .insight-box h3 {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .fail-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>